      the instances actually know.  Five hearsays (c = 0.23 each) become c_i = 0.74 and c_g = 0.83 (tau_inf = 1, cap = 1);
      without the loop the same five hearsays give c_i = 0.47.

   'accumulate' semantics (C3: evidence is ADDED at every moment), m = 3, tau_inf = 0.5, cap = 1:
   t=1: W_i= 0.52 c_i=0.344 | t=2: W_i= 0.92 c_i=0.479 | t=5: W_i= 3.11 c_i=0.757 | t=10: W_i= 6.86 c_i=0.873 | t=20: W_i=14.36 c_i=0.935

== b. reading B (no loop: Up sees own evidence only).  Own evidence still comes back, and categories with
      the same members (§3: every frame slot creates a NEW category unit for its fillers) are summed. ==
   10 instances, each one own sensed observation (W = 1), cap = 1, e(i->g) = 1
   duplicate categories D   W_eff(design)   c_eff    own share returned   | corrected (best route, LOO, coupling 1): W_eff  c
          1                  6.0      0.857         0.5 units        |    1.90  0.655
          2                 11.0      0.917         1.0 units        |    1.90  0.655
          5                 26.0      0.963         2.5 units        |    1.90  0.655
         10                 51.0      0.981         5.0 units        |    1.90  0.655
         30                151.0      0.993        15.0 units        |    1.90  0.655
   -> conviction grows with the number of sentence frames the same fillers were met in, not with evidence.

== c. the cap is bypassed.  ONE instance i of g is observed n times with v (sensed).  g is in the focus
      each time (activated through ABSTRACT, a_g = e(i->g) = 1), so LEARN writes g -> v directly. ==
   n     W(g->v) by Up (cap 1)   W(g->v) with LEARN on g   a NEVER OBSERVED j inherits   c_j     e_j
      1          1.0                      2.0                   1.0            0.500  0.750
     10          1.0                     11.0                   5.5            0.846  0.923
    100          1.0                    101.0                  50.5            0.981  0.990
   1000          1.0                   1001.0                 500.5            0.998  0.999
   -> one member seen a thousand times makes the mind 99.8% convinced about every other member.

== d. 'an exception stays an exception'.  m members hold v (each W+ >= cap = 1); member x is SEEN not to. ==
   own contrary sensed observations x needs before e_eff(x -> v) < 1/2:
   m      design (n- > lambda(m-1))   corrected, bounded (coupling 1)   corrected, gated (A_g = 0.9)
      2              1                            1                                1
      5              3                            1                                1
     10              5                            1                                1
     20             10                            1                                1
    100             50                            1                                1
   1000            500                            1                                1
   design, m = 20, after ONE sighting that x is not v: W+ = 10.0, W- = 1.5, f = 0.87, c = 0.92, e = 0.84  (the mind does not believe its eyes)

== e. generated worlds.  Category rule mu in {0.95, 0.05}; a member conforms with probability q, otherwise it is
      the opposite (theta = 1 - mu).  Own sensed observations per member n in {0,1,2,3,5,10}.  300 categories. ==
   mean squared error of e_eff against the member's true frequency theta (lower is better)
   dB = design, Up sees own evidence (reading B) | dA = design, Up sees inherited evidence too (loop, reading A)
   corrected: base = base rate only (learned horizon; base1 = horizon 1) | bnd = + evidence bounded by 1 |
              lrn = bounded by learned conformity |
              gat = bounded by this member's conformity | gat(b=1/2) = gated without the base rate
