   -> the design gets WORSE as the category grows; exceptions with ten own observations are still overruled
      (m = 100, q = 0.9: 0.42 against 0.006 for own evidence alone).  In the q = 0.5 world (no usable rule)
      the design is worse than ignoring categories altogether: a large mixed category overwrites what each
      member knows about itself with unbounded 50/50 evidence.
